--------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE ON THE TRAINING DATA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The datasets under `data/` are derived from digitized editions of classical
Arabic hadith collections. The underlying works are centuries old and in the
public domain. The particular digitizations and modern critical editions from
which the text was harvested may carry editorial rights in some
jurisdictions; the excerpts retained here are short, non-contiguous windows
kept for research and reproducibility. See `docs/DATA.md` for provenance
details. If you intend to redistribute the datasets commercially, review the
position of the source editions in your own jurisdiction.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The optional silver-label teacher in `src/arabicmodels/teachers/` calls
CAMeL Tools, which is distributed separately under the MIT License and is not
bundled with this product:

    CAMeL Tools — https://github.com/CAMeL-Lab/camel_tools
    Copyright (c) 2018-2024 New York University Abu Dhabi

The POS dataset in `data/pos.jsonl` contains silver labels produced by that
tool. Training and inference with the shipped models do not require it.
